WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.870
A teacher types test marks into a program,

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.210
one at a time.

3
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.010
Nobody has told the program how
many students are in the class.

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.750
Yet when she's finished, the
screen shows the class average.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.910
An average needs a division.

6
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.110
So how can a program divide
by a number it was never told?

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.890
In this mission, you'll
keep a running total.

8
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.875
Set it to 0 before the loop,
then add each new mark:

9
00:00:24.925 --> 00:00:29.650
12, 7, 9 and 15 take it to 43.

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:34.950
You'll also meet counting: something
that adds 1 each time a thing happens.

11
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.670
Your mission: work out how the program
gets the average right without being told

12
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.400
how many.
